# Fixture: map_found_colony start (France 1599, human = French, view origin (35,17)); English Cayenne (38,23) holds 2 colonists (colonist 0 in a building).
# Enter on a foreign colony (port_bugs.md #1566): DOS FUN_2b5a_32ee / 3344 (raw 45879 / 45903) open the colony screen only when its owner is the
# viewpoint nation (DS:0x5396) or Complete Map (DS:0x53a2) is on. Right-click puts the map in View mode with the cursor on Cayenne (origin -> (31,17)).
# 1) Enter without Complete Map: nothing opens. 2) CHEAT Reveal Map > Complete Map, cheat mode off again (the gate is DS:0x53a2, not the CHEAT bit),
# Enter: Cayenne's screen opens; colonist 0 is dragged from its building onto the free plot N (260,43): a Farmer there.
# Saved: show_entire_map 1 + show_indian_moves off (Complete Map pick); View mode (map_mode 1, no unit selected, cursor/viewport on Cayenne);
# colonies[7] occupation[0] 13 -> 0 (Farmer), tiles[0] -1 -> 0 (plot N); map mask (38,22) |= 0x10, the worked-plot bit every seat stamps
# (FUN_0000_6518(dx,dy,1), FUN_0000_6582 raw 8833). (38,22) is not tribal land, so no purchase / alarm.
rclick 56 112            # View mode, cursor on Cayenne (38,23)
wait 2
key Return               # not ours, no Complete Map: nothing opens
wait 3
shot
key w alt
key i alt
key n alt
key F4 shift             # Reveal Map (bar on Complete Map, #1661)
key Return               # Complete Map
wait 2
key w alt                # cheat mode off; Complete Map stays
wait 2
key Return               # Cayenne's colony screen opens
wait 3
shot
drag 5 155 260 43        # colonist 0 (people strip) -> free plot N: Farmer
wait 2
shot
key Escape               # back to the map
wait 3
shot
